    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Seljuk sultanate that ruled central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konya">Konya</a> for over two centuries after the Byzantine defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manzikert">Manzikert</a>.</li><li>Its sultans built a Persianate court and a trade network of ports and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravanserai">caravanserais</a> linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>.</li><li>Defeat by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kose-dag">Köse Dağ</a> in 1243 made it a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> state, and it dissolved into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beyliks</a> that included the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> of Rum built more than a hundred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravanserai">caravanserais</a> along <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>’s roads, some so large and fortified that they resemble castles.</p></aside>
    </section>

